steps {
  type: CORTEX_STEP_TYPE_USER_INPUT
  status: CORTEX_STEP_STATUS_DONE
  metadata {
    created_at {
      seconds: 1787269971
      nanos: 112069270
    }
    source: CORTEX_STEP_SOURCE_USER_EXPLICIT
  }
  user_input {
    user_response: "# MASTER PROMPT \342\200\224 FULL WEBSITE AUDIT + 100% PRODUCTION FIX\n\n**Act as a senior CTO, full-stack engineer, DevOps engineer, security engineer, QA engineer, and UX engineer. Perform a complete end-to-end audit of this entire web application and fix every detectable issue. Do not redesign or remove existing functionality unless absolutely necessary. The goal is a genuinely production-ready, deployable, fully functional application.**\n\n## 1. COMPLETE CODEBASE AUDIT\n\nAudit **every file, folder, component, page, API, function, dependency, configuration, database connection, environment variable, and deployment setting**.\n\nCheck for:\n\n* Build errors\n* Runtime errors\n* TypeScript errors\n* JavaScript errors\n* React errors\n* Missing imports\n* Incorrect imports\n* Unused/broken dependencies\n* Dependency version conflicts\n* Deprecated APIs\n* Broken components\n* Broken buttons\n* Broken forms\n* Broken navigation\n* Broken links\n* Missing routes\n* Incorrect routes\n* 404 pages\n* Console errors\n* Network errors\n* API errors\n* CORS errors\n* Authentication problems\n* Authorization problems\n* Database errors\n* State-management bugs\n* Loading-state bugs\n* Empty-state bugs\n* Error-state bugs\n* Race conditions\n* Memory leaks\n* Hydration errors\n* SSR/CSR problems\n* Responsive layout problems\n* Accessibility issues\n* Performance problems\n* Security vulnerabilities\n\n**Do not stop after finding the first issue. Audit the entire application.**\n\n---\n\n# 2. TEST EVERY PAGE\n\nCreate a complete page inventory.\n\nFor every page verify:\n\n* Page loads\n* URL works\n* Navigation works\n* Back button works\n* Refresh works\n* Direct URL access works\n* Mobile layout works\n* Tablet layout works\n* Desktop layout works\n* Images load\n* Fonts load\n* Icons load\n* Animations work\n* Forms work\n* Buttons work\n* Modals work\n* Dropdowns work\n* Search works\n* Filters work\n* Pagination works\n* Authentication works\n* Data loads correctly\n* Error handling works\n\nFix every broken page.\n\n---\n\n# 3. TEST EVERY BUTTON\n\n**Every visible button must perform a real action.**\n\nDo not leave:\n\n* Fake buttons\n* Placeholder buttons\n* Dead buttons\n* `console.log()` actions\n* Empty click handlers\n* TODO actions\n* Demo-only functionality\n\nFor every button determine its intended behavior and implement it.\n\nExamples:\n\n**Import Project \342\206\222** actually import project\n\n**Analyze \342\206\222** actually analyze project\n\n**Build \342\206\222** actually build project\n\n**Fix \342\206\222** actually apply fixes\n\n**Download \342\206\222** actually generate and download the correct file\n\n**Delete \342\206\222** actually delete after confirmation\n\n**Retry \342\206\222** actually retry the failed operation\n\n**Copy \342\206\222** actually copy content\n\n**Preview \342\206\222** actually open the preview\n\n---\n\n# 4. WEBSITE \342\206\222 HOSTINGER CONVERTER AUDIT\n\nBecause this application converts projects into Hostinger-ready deployments, specifically test the complete pipeline:\n\n```text\nINPUT\n\342\206\223\nIMPORT\n\342\206\223\nPROJECT DETECTION\n\342\206\223\nSOURCE ANALYSIS\n\342\206\223\nFRAMEWORK DETECTION\n\342\206\223\nDEPENDENCY ANALYSIS\n\342\206\223\nENVIRONMENT ANALYSIS\n\342\206\223\nBUILD\n\342\206\223\nERROR DETECTION\n\342\206\223\nAUTOMATIC REPAIR\n\342\206\223\nPRODUCTION BUILD\n\342\206\223\nDEPLOYMENT VALIDATION\n\342\206\223\nPACKAGE GENERATION\n\342\206\223\nZIP CREATION\n\342\206\223\nDOWNLOAD\n```\n\nEvery stage must actually work.\n\n---\n\n# 5. IMPORT SYSTEM\n\nTest all supported input methods.\n\n### URL\n\n* AI Studio\n* Lovable\n* Replit\n* GitHub\n* Public website URL\n\n### Files\n\n* ZIP\n* Project folder\n* Individual source files\n\nValidate:\n\n* Invalid URL\n* Private URL\n* Expired URL\n* Inaccessible URL\n* Invalid ZIP\n* Corrupted ZIP\n* Empty project\n* Unsupported project\n* Missing source code\n\nShow useful error messages instead of crashing.\n\n---\n\n# 6. PROJECT DETECTION\n\nAutomatically identify:\n\n* HTML\n* CSS\n* JavaScript\n* TypeScript\n* React\n* Vite\n* Next.js\n* Vue\n* Angular\n* Svelte\n* Node.js\n* PHP\n* Static sites\n* Other supported frameworks\n\nDetect:\n\n* `package.json`\n* lock files\n* build configuration\n* source directory\n* public directory\n* backend\n* API routes\n* database\n* environment variables\n\n---\n\n# 7. BACKEND FUNCTIONALITY\n\nDo not destroy backend functionality simply to make the frontend deploy.\n\nDetect:\n\n* Node.js\n* API routes\n* Server actions\n* Serverless functions\n* PHP\n* Databases\n* Authentication\n* File storage\n* Webhooks\n* Cron jobs\n* AI APIs\n* Payment APIs\n\nIf Hostinger compatibility requires changes, create a clear migration plan.\n\n---\n\n# 8. ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES\n\nScan the entire project for:\n\n* API keys\n* database URLs\n* authentication secrets\n* private tokens\n* payment secrets\n* third-party credentials\n\nNever expose secrets in frontend bundles.\n\nGenerate:\n\n`.env.example`\n\nand clearly identify required variables.\n\nFix incorrect:\n\n* `localhost`\n* development URLs\n* API URLs\n* environment references\n\n---\n\n# 9. HOSTINGER COMPATIBILITY\n\nTest the generated project against the selected deployment type.\n\n### Static\n\nVerify:\n\n* `index.html`\n* assets\n* routes\n* SPA fallback\n* `.htaccess`\n* production paths\n\n### Node.js\n\nVerify:\n\n* `package.json`\n* start command\n* production environment\n* port configuration\n* server entry point\n* dependencies\n\n### PHP\n\nVerify PHP entry points and required configuration.\n\nNever claim compatibility without actually validating it.\n\n---\n\n# 10. AUTOMATIC REPAIR ENGINE\n\nFix all safe, detectable issues automatically.\n\nExamples:\n\n```text\n\342\234\223 Fixed broken imports\n\342\234\223 Installed missing dependencies\n\342\234\223 Fixed asset paths\n\342\234\223 Fixed routing\n\342\234\223 Fixed production configuration\n\342\234\223 Removed localhost references\n\342\234\223 Fixed build configuration\n\342\234\223 Fixed environment configuration\n\342\234\223 Added SPA fallback\n\342\234\223 Fixed case-sensitive paths\n\342\234\223 Fixed broken links\n```\n\nAfter every repair, run the relevant tests again.\n\n**Never assume a fix worked. Verify it.**\n\n---\n\n# 11. BUILD VERIFICATION\n\nRun a clean production build from scratch.\n\nCheck:\n\n* Install\n* Dependency resolution\n* Type checking\n* Linting\n* Build\n* Production start\n* Route loading\n* API connectivity\n* Static assets\n* Runtime behavior\n\nIf the build fails:\n\n1. Capture the exact error.\n2. Identify the root cause.\n3. Fix it.\n4. Rebuild.\n5. Repeat until no safe, actionable errors remain.\n\n---\n\n# 12. SECURITY AUDIT\n\nPerform a complete security audit.\n\nCheck for:\n\n* XSS\n* CSRF\n* SSRF\n* SQL injection\n* command injection\n* path traversal\n* insecure file uploads\n* malicious ZIP files\n* exposed secrets\n* insecure authentication\n* broken authorization\n* unsafe redirects\n* insecure CORS\n* vulnerable dependencies\n* unsafe URL fetching\n* arbitrary code execution\n\nImported projects must be processed in an **isolated/sandboxed build environment**.\n\nNever execute untrusted project code directly inside the main application server.\n\n---\n\n# 13. PERFORMANCE AUDIT\n\nOptimize without breaking functionality.\n\nCheck:\n\n* Bundle size\n* JavaScript size\n* CSS size\n* Images\n* Fonts\n* Lazy loading\n* Code splitting\n* Caching\n* API requests\n* Duplicate requests\n* Rendering performance\n* Memory usage\n\nRemove unnecessary dependencies and code only when safe.\n\n---\n\n# 14. MOBILE + RESPONSIVE AUDIT\n\nTest:\n\n### Mobile\n\n320px, 375px, 390px, 414px\n\n### Tablet\n\n768px, 1024px\n\n### Desktop\n\n1280px, 1440px, 1920px\n\nFix:\n\n* Horizontal scrolling\n* Overflow\n* Broken grids\n* Tiny text\n* Overlapping elements\n* Broken modals\n* Broken navigation\n* Touch targets\n* Mobile menus\n* Responsive tables\n\n---\n\n# 15. ACCESSIBILITY AUDIT\n\nCheck:\n\n* Keyboard navigation\n* Focus states\n* Labels\n* ARIA\n* Color contrast\n* Semantic HTML\n* Form errors\n* Screen-reader compatibility\n* Image alt text\n* Button accessibility\n\nFix all practical accessibility issues.\n\n---\n\n# 16. UX AUDIT\n\nEvery operation must have:\n\n### Loading state\n\n```text\nAnalyzing project...\n```\n\n### Success state\n\n```text\nProject successfully analyzed.\n```\n\n### Error state\n\n```text\nUnable to analyze this project.\nReason: ...\nHow to fix: ...\n```\n\n### Empty state\n\n```text\nNo projects yet.\nImport your first project.\n```\n\nNever leave the user staring at a blank screen.\n\n---\n\n# 17. ERROR HANDLING\n\nImplement centralized error handling.\n\nErrors must be:\n\n* Captured\n* Logged\n* Categorized\n* Displayed clearly\n* Recoverable where possible\n\nNever expose sensitive server errors to users.\n\nNever silently swallow errors.\n\n---\n\n# 18. DATABASE AUDIT\n\nIf a database exists, verify:\n\n* Connection\n* Schema\n* Queries\n* Migrations\n* Validation\n* Error handling\n* Permissions\n* Indexes\n* Connection pooling\n* Production configuration\n\nTest:\n\n**Create \342\206\222 Read \342\206\222 Update \342\206\222 Delete**\n\nfor every important entity.\n\n---\n\n# 19. AUTHENTICATION AUDIT\n\nTest:\n\n* Sign up\n* Login\n* Logout\n* Session persistence\n* Password reset\n* Protected routes\n* Unauthorized access\n* Expired sessions\n* User permissions\n\nMake sure users cannot access another user\'s projects or files.\n\n---\n\n# 20. DOWNLOAD SYSTEM\n\nTest the final package.\n\nThe ZIP must:\n\n* Actually exist\n* Open correctly\n* Contain all required files\n* Preserve folder structure\n* Contain production files\n* Not contain unnecessary development files\n* Include `.env.example`\n* Include deployment instructions\n* Include conversion report\n\nActually test extracting the ZIP before declaring success.\n\n---\n\n# 21. FINAL DEPLOYMENT VALIDATION\n\nPerform a clean end-to-end test:\n\n```text\nCreate/import project\n\342\206\223\nAnalyze\n\342\206\223\nFix\n\342\206\223\nBuild\n\342\206\223\nValidate\n\342\206\223\nPackage\n\342\206\223\nExtract ZIP\n\342\206\223\nInstall dependencies if required\n\342\206\223\nStart production environment\n\342\206\223\nOpen website\n\342\206\223\nTest routes\n\342\206\223\nTest major functions\n\342\206\223\nConfirm no critical errors\n```\n\n---\n\n# 22. FINAL AUDIT REPORT\n\nCreate a professional report containing:\n\n### Overall Status\n\n**PRODUCTION READY**\n\nor\n\n**ACTION REQUIRED**\n\nNever display \342\200\234100% working\342\200\235 unless the system has actually verified the required functionality.\n\nShow:\n\n```text\nPages Tested:          24/24\nButtons Tested:       86/86\nRoutes Tested:        31/31\nAPIs Tested:          18/18\nBuild:                PASS\nRuntime:              PASS\nSecurity:             PASS\nMobile:               PASS\nDesktop:              PASS\nDownload Package:     PASS\nHostinger Validation: PASS\nCritical Errors:      0\n```\n\n---\n\n# 23. ZERO PLACEHOLDER POLICY\n\nSearch the entire codebase for:\n\n* TODO\n* FIXME\n* Coming Soon\n* Placeholder\n* Demo\n* Mock\n* Fake data\n* Dummy API\n* `console.log`\n* Empty functions\n* Unimplemented handlers\n\nReplace every production-relevant placeholder with a real implementation or clearly mark it as unsupported functionality.\n\n---\n\n# 24. FINAL REQUIREMENT\n\n**Do not merely tell me what is wrong. FIX IT.**\n\nAfter fixing each issue:\n\n**TEST \342\206\222 VERIFY \342\206\222 FIX \342\206\222 RETEST**\n\nContinue until the application reaches the highest genuinely verifiable production-readiness level.\n\nDo not remove existing features just to make tests pass.\n\nDo not replace functional systems with fake/mock implementations.\n\nDo not claim success without verification.\n\n**Final objective: a complete, secure, responsive, stable, production-ready website-to-Hostinger deployment application with every supported function working end-to-end.**"
    items {
      text: "# MASTER PROMPT \342\200\224 FULL WEBSITE AUDIT + 100% PRODUCTION FIX\n\n**Act as a senior CTO, full-stack engineer, DevOps engineer, security engineer, QA engineer, and UX engineer. Perform a complete end-to-end audit of this entire web application and fix every detectable issue. Do not redesign or remove existing functionality unless absolutely necessary. The goal is a genuinely production-ready, deployable, fully functional application.**\n\n## 1. COMPLETE CODEBASE AUDIT\n\nAudit **every file, folder, component, page, API, function, dependency, configuration, database connection, environment variable, and deployment setting**.\n\nCheck for:\n\n* Build errors\n* Runtime errors\n* TypeScript errors\n* JavaScript errors\n* React errors\n* Missing imports\n* Incorrect imports\n* Unused/broken dependencies\n* Dependency version conflicts\n* Deprecated APIs\n* Broken components\n* Broken buttons\n* Broken forms\n* Broken navigation\n* Broken links\n* Missing routes\n* Incorrect routes\n* 404 pages\n* Console errors\n* Network errors\n* API errors\n* CORS errors\n* Authentication problems\n* Authorization problems\n* Database errors\n* State-management bugs\n* Loading-state bugs\n* Empty-state bugs\n* Error-state bugs\n* Race conditions\n* Memory leaks\n* Hydration errors\n* SSR/CSR problems\n* Responsive layout problems\n* Accessibility issues\n* Performance problems\n* Security vulnerabilities\n\n**Do not stop after finding the first issue. Audit the entire application.**\n\n---\n\n# 2. TEST EVERY PAGE\n\nCreate a complete page inventory.\n\nFor every page verify:\n\n* Page loads\n* URL works\n* Navigation works\n* Back button works\n* Refresh works\n* Direct URL access works\n* Mobile layout works\n* Tablet layout works\n* Desktop layout works\n* Images load\n* Fonts load\n* Icons load\n* Animations work\n* Forms work\n* Buttons work\n* Modals work\n* Dropdowns work\n* Search works\n* Filters work\n* Pagination works\n* Authentication works\n* Data loads correctly\n* Error handling works\n\nFix every broken page.\n\n---\n\n# 3. TEST EVERY BUTTON\n\n**Every visible button must perform a real action.**\n\nDo not leave:\n\n* Fake buttons\n* Placeholder buttons\n* Dead buttons\n* `console.log()` actions\n* Empty click handlers\n* TODO actions\n* Demo-only functionality\n\nFor every button determine its intended behavior and implement it.\n\nExamples:\n\n**Import Project \342\206\222** actually import project\n\n**Analyze \342\206\222** actually analyze project\n\n**Build \342\206\222** actually build project\n\n**Fix \342\206\222** actually apply fixes\n\n**Download \342\206\222** actually generate and download the correct file\n\n**Delete \342\206\222** actually delete after confirmation\n\n**Retry \342\206\222** actually retry the failed operation\n\n**Copy \342\206\222** actually copy content\n\n**Preview \342\206\222** actually open the preview\n\n---\n\n# 4. WEBSITE \342\206\222 HOSTINGER CONVERTER AUDIT\n\nBecause this application converts projects into Hostinger-ready deployments, specifically test the complete pipeline:\n\n```text\nINPUT\n\342\206\223\nIMPORT\n\342\206\223\nPROJECT DETECTION\n\342\206\223\nSOURCE ANALYSIS\n\342\206\223\nFRAMEWORK DETECTION\n\342\206\223\nDEPENDENCY ANALYSIS\n\342\206\223\nENVIRONMENT ANALYSIS\n\342\206\223\nBUILD\n\342\206\223\nERROR DETECTION\n\342\206\223\nAUTOMATIC REPAIR\n\342\206\223\nPRODUCTION BUILD\n\342\206\223\nDEPLOYMENT VALIDATION\n\342\206\223\nPACKAGE GENERATION\n\342\206\223\nZIP CREATION\n\342\206\223\nDOWNLOAD\n```\n\nEvery stage must actually work.\n\n---\n\n# 5. IMPORT SYSTEM\n\nTest all supported input methods.\n\n### URL\n\n* AI Studio\n* Lovable\n* Replit\n* GitHub\n* Public website URL\n\n### Files\n\n* ZIP\n* Project folder\n* Individual source files\n\nValidate:\n\n* Invalid URL\n* Private URL\n* Expired URL\n* Inaccessible URL\n* Invalid ZIP\n* Corrupted ZIP\n* Empty project\n* Unsupported project\n* Missing source code\n\nShow useful error messages instead of crashing.\n\n---\n\n# 6. PROJECT DETECTION\n\nAutomatically identify:\n\n* HTML\n* CSS\n* JavaScript\n* TypeScript\n* React\n* Vite\n* Next.js\n* Vue\n* Angular\n* Svelte\n* Node.js\n* PHP\n* Static sites\n* Other supported frameworks\n\nDetect:\n\n* `package.json`\n* lock files\n* build configuration\n* source directory\n* public directory\n* backend\n* API routes\n* database\n* environment variables\n\n---\n\n# 7. BACKEND FUNCTIONALITY\n\nDo not destroy backend functionality simply to make the frontend deploy.\n\nDetect:\n\n* Node.js\n* API routes\n* Server actions\n* Serverless functions\n* PHP\n* Databases\n* Authentication\n* File storage\n* Webhooks\n* Cron jobs\n* AI APIs\n* Payment APIs\n\nIf Hostinger compatibility requires changes, create a clear migration plan.\n\n---\n\n# 8. ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES\n\nScan the entire project for:\n\n* API keys\n* database URLs\n* authentication secrets\n* private tokens\n* payment secrets\n* third-party credentials\n\nNever expose secrets in frontend bundles.\n\nGenerate:\n\n`.env.example`\n\nand clearly identify required variables.\n\nFix incorrect:\n\n* `localhost`\n* development URLs\n* API URLs\n* environment references\n\n---\n\n# 9. HOSTINGER COMPATIBILITY\n\nTest the generated project against the selected deployment type.\n\n### Static\n\nVerify:\n\n* `index.html`\n* assets\n* routes\n* SPA fallback\n* `.htaccess`\n* production paths\n\n### Node.js\n\nVerify:\n\n* `package.json`\n* start command\n* production environment\n* port configuration\n* server entry point\n* dependencies\n\n### PHP\n\nVerify PHP entry points and required configuration.\n\nNever claim compatibility without actually validating it.\n\n---\n\n# 10. AUTOMATIC REPAIR ENGINE\n\nFix all safe, detectable issues automatically.\n\nExamples:\n\n```text\n\342\234\223 Fixed broken imports\n\342\234\223 Installed missing dependencies\n\342\234\223 Fixed asset paths\n\342\234\223 Fixed routing\n\342\234\223 Fixed production configuration\n\342\234\223 Removed localhost references\n\342\234\223 Fixed build configuration\n\342\234\223 Fixed environment configuration\n\342\234\223 Added SPA fallback\n\342\234\223 Fixed case-sensitive paths\n\342\234\223 Fixed broken links\n```\n\nAfter every repair, run the relevant tests again.\n\n**Never assume a fix worked. Verify it.**\n\n---\n\n# 11. BUILD VERIFICATION\n\nRun a clean production build from scratch.\n\nCheck:\n\n* Install\n* Dependency resolution\n* Type checking\n* Linting\n* Build\n* Production start\n* Route loading\n* API connectivity\n* Static assets\n* Runtime behavior\n\nIf the build fails:\n\n1. Capture the exact error.\n2. Identify the root cause.\n3. Fix it.\n4. Rebuild.\n5. Repeat until no safe, actionable errors remain.\n\n---\n\n# 12. SECURITY AUDIT\n\nPerform a complete security audit.\n\nCheck for:\n\n* XSS\n* CSRF\n* SSRF\n* SQL injection\n* command injection\n* path traversal\n* insecure file uploads\n* malicious ZIP files\n* exposed secrets\n* insecure authentication\n* broken authorization\n* unsafe redirects\n* insecure CORS\n* vulnerable dependencies\n* unsafe URL fetching\n* arbitrary code execution\n\nImported projects must be processed in an **isolated/sandboxed build environment**.\n\nNever execute untrusted project code directly inside the main application server.\n\n---\n\n# 13. PERFORMANCE AUDIT\n\nOptimize without breaking functionality.\n\nCheck:\n\n* Bundle size\n* JavaScript size\n* CSS size\n* Images\n* Fonts\n* Lazy loading\n* Code splitting\n* Caching\n* API requests\n* Duplicate requests\n* Rendering performance\n* Memory usage\n\nRemove unnecessary dependencies and code only when safe.\n\n---\n\n# 14. MOBILE + RESPONSIVE AUDIT\n\nTest:\n\n### Mobile\n\n320px, 375px, 390px, 414px\n\n### Tablet\n\n768px, 1024px\n\n### Desktop\n\n1280px, 1440px, 1920px\n\nFix:\n\n* Horizontal scrolling\n* Overflow\n* Broken grids\n* Tiny text\n* Overlapping elements\n* Broken modals\n* Broken navigation\n* Touch targets\n* Mobile menus\n* Responsive tables\n\n---\n\n# 15. ACCESSIBILITY AUDIT\n\nCheck:\n\n* Keyboard navigation\n* Focus states\n* Labels\n* ARIA\n* Color contrast\n* Semantic HTML\n* Form errors\n* Screen-reader compatibility\n* Image alt text\n* Button accessibility\n\nFix all practical accessibility issues.\n\n---\n\n# 16. UX AUDIT\n\nEvery operation must have:\n\n### Loading state\n\n```text\nAnalyzing project...\n```\n\n### Success state\n\n```text\nProject successfully analyzed.\n```\n\n### Error state\n\n```text\nUnable to analyze this project.\nReason: ...\nHow to fix: ...\n```\n\n### Empty state\n\n```text\nNo projects yet.\nImport your first project.\n```\n\nNever leave the user staring at a blank screen.\n\n---\n\n# 17. ERROR HANDLING\n\nImplement centralized error handling.\n\nErrors must be:\n\n* Captured\n* Logged\n* Categorized\n* Displayed clearly\n* Recoverable where possible\n\nNever expose sensitive server errors to users.\n\nNever silently swallow errors.\n\n---\n\n# 18. DATABASE AUDIT\n\nIf a database exists, verify:\n\n* Connection\n* Schema\n* Queries\n* Migrations\n* Validation\n* Error handling\n* Permissions\n* Indexes\n* Connection pooling\n* Production configuration\n\nTest:\n\n**Create \342\206\222 Read \342\206\222 Update \342\206\222 Delete**\n\nfor every important entity.\n\n---\n\n# 19. AUTHENTICATION AUDIT\n\nTest:\n\n* Sign up\n* Login\n* Logout\n* Session persistence\n* Password reset\n* Protected routes\n* Unauthorized access\n* Expired sessions\n* User permissions\n\nMake sure users cannot access another user\'s projects or files.\n\n---\n\n# 20. DOWNLOAD SYSTEM\n\nTest the final package.\n\nThe ZIP must:\n\n* Actually exist\n* Open correctly\n* Contain all required files\n* Preserve folder structure\n* Contain production files\n* Not contain unnecessary development files\n* Include `.env.example`\n* Include deployment instructions\n* Include conversion report\n\nActually test extracting the ZIP before declaring success.\n\n---\n\n# 21. FINAL DEPLOYMENT VALIDATION\n\nPerform a clean end-to-end test:\n\n```text\nCreate/import project\n\342\206\223\nAnalyze\n\342\206\223\nFix\n\342\206\223\nBuild\n\342\206\223\nValidate\n\342\206\223\nPackage\n\342\206\223\nExtract ZIP\n\342\206\223\nInstall dependencies if required\n\342\206\223\nStart production environment\n\342\206\223\nOpen website\n\342\206\223\nTest routes\n\342\206\223\nTest major functions\n\342\206\223\nConfirm no critical errors\n```\n\n---\n\n# 22. FINAL AUDIT REPORT\n\nCreate a professional report containing:\n\n### Overall Status\n\n**PRODUCTION READY**\n\nor\n\n**ACTION REQUIRED**\n\nNever display \342\200\234100% working\342\200\235 unless the system has actually verified the required functionality.\n\nShow:\n\n```text\nPages Tested:          24/24\nButtons Tested:       86/86\nRoutes Tested:        31/31\nAPIs Tested:          18/18\nBuild:                PASS\nRuntime:              PASS\nSecurity:             PASS\nMobile:               PASS\nDesktop:              PASS\nDownload Package:     PASS\nHostinger Validation: PASS\nCritical Errors:      0\n```\n\n---\n\n# 23. ZERO PLACEHOLDER POLICY\n\nSearch the entire codebase for:\n\n* TODO\n* FIXME\n* Coming Soon\n* Placeholder\n* Demo\n* Mock\n* Fake data\n* Dummy API\n* `console.log`\n* Empty functions\n* Unimplemented handlers\n\nReplace every production-relevant placeholder with a real implementation or clearly mark it as unsupported functionality.\n\n---\n\n# 24. FINAL REQUIREMENT\n\n**Do not merely tell me what is wrong. FIX IT.**\n\nAfter fixing each issue:\n\n**TEST \342\206\222 VERIFY \342\206\222 FIX \342\206\222 RETEST**\n\nContinue until the application reaches the highest genuinely verifiable production-readiness level.\n\nDo not remove existing features just to make tests pass.\n\nDo not replace functional systems with fake/mock implementations.\n\nDo not claim success without verification.\n\n**Final objective: a complete, secure, responsive, stable, production-ready website-to-Hostinger deployment application with every supported function working end-to-end.**"
    }
  }
}
