  planner_response {
    response: "I have completed the end-to-end audit, branding transition to **GoDeploy**, and Bento Grid design implementation across the entire application:\n\n- **Branding & Visual Identity**: Updated the application identity to **GoDeploy** across the entire stack, including `metadata.json`, HTML meta tags, top navigation, sidebar, pipeline views, packaging scripts, and generated reports. Implemented a custom SVG vector logo featuring an indigo/violet rocket badge with clean typography.\n- **Bento Grid Architecture**: Refined all workflow stages (**Import**, **Analyze**, **Repair**, **Build**, **Validate**, **Download**, and **Live Preview**) into cohesive Bento Grid modules with dark slate cards, radial gauges, status indicators, and responsive breakpoints.\n- **End-to-End Conversion Pipeline**:\n  - **Import Engine**: Supports drag-and-drop ZIP archive uploads, directory imports, remote URL DOM fetching with SSRF protection, and pre-configured sample templates.\n  - **Analysis & Repair Engine**: Detects frameworks, routing strategies, environment variables, and static assets; automatically fixes hardcoded `localhost` references, generates production-grade LiteSpeed/Apache `.htaccess` rewrite rules, and normalizes file paths for Hostinger `public_html`.\n  - **AI Architecture Audit**: Connected to Gemini 3.7 Flash via `/api/ai-audit` to evaluate hosting tiers and potential deployment pitfalls.\n  - **Packaging & Validator**: Compiles download-ready ZIP bundles with automated `robots.txt`, `sitemap.xml`, `.env.example`, and comprehensive HTML audit reports.\n  - **Live Simulator**: Renders sandboxed previews across Desktop, Tablet, and Mobile device frames.\n- **Verification**: Executed both type checking (`tsc --noEmit`) and the production build pipeline (`vite build` + backend bundle), confirming zero errors."
    thinking: "**Verifying Project Consistency**\n\nOkay, I\'m currently focused on meticulous file checks to guarantee complete consistency. \"GoDeploy\" branding needs to be spotless. I am also making sure the modern Bento Grid UI is implemented correctly, with zero broken links, buttons, or placeholders.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I have completed the end-to-end audit, branding transition to **GoDeploy**, and Bento Grid design implementation across the entire application:\n\n- **Branding & Visual Identity**: Updated the application identity to **GoDeploy** across the entire stack, including `metadata.json`, HTML meta tags, top navigation, sidebar, pipeline views, packaging scripts, and generated reports. Implemented a custom SVG vector logo featuring an indigo/violet rocket badge with clean typography.\n- **Bento Grid Architecture**: Refined all workflow stages (**Import**, **Analyze**, **Repair**, **Build**, **Validate**, **Download**, and **Live Preview**) into cohesive Bento Grid modules with dark slate cards, radial gauges, status indicators, and responsive breakpoints.\n- **End-to-End Conversion Pipeline**:\n  - **Import Engine**: Supports drag-and-drop ZIP archive uploads, directory imports, remote URL DOM fetching with SSRF protection, and pre-configured sample templates.\n  - **Analysis & Repair Engine**: Detects frameworks, routing strategies, environment variables, and static assets; automatically fixes hardcoded `localhost` references, generates production-grade LiteSpeed/Apache `.htaccess` rewrite rules, and normalizes file paths for Hostinger `public_html`.\n  - **AI Architecture Audit**: Connected to Gemini 3.7 Flash via `/api/ai-audit` to evaluate hosting tiers and potential deployment pitfalls.\n  - **Packaging & Validator**: Compiles download-ready ZIP bundles with automated `robots.txt`, `sitemap.xml`, `.env.example`, and comprehensive HTML audit reports.\n  - **Live Simulator**: Renders sandboxed previews across Desktop, Tablet, and Mobile device frames.\n- **Verification**: Executed both type checking (`tsc --noEmit`) and the production build pipeline (`vite build` + backend bundle), confirming zero errors."
