  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing User Interaction**\n\nOkay, I\'m examining the scenario where a user imports a site or enters an app URL. I\'m focusing on the user actions and their effects. I\'m analyzing the screenshot the user provided to understand the import process and related issues. This helps me understand the complete process.\n\n\n**Investigating Scaling Issues**\n\nI\'ve been looking deeper into the `PreviewView.tsx` component and the `srcDocContent` generation. Specifically, I\'m focusing on how the content, whether imported or native, is rendered within the mobile preview frame. It seems when the device is mobile, the 375px frame leads to potential overflows or improper scaling, possibly because of missing viewport meta tags or a lack of mobile-responsive styling in the imported content, or even scraping of the GoDeploy UI, and rendering it directly in the small frame. I need to understand this better.\n\n\n**Pinpointing Viewport Problems**\n\nI\'m now focusing on how viewport issues cause problems. I see that if the HTML lacks the `<meta name=\"viewport\">` tag or the iframe does not handle scaling, content overflows in the mobile preview. The fixed 375px width in mobile mode is a key factor. Also, in the screenshot, the webpage in the iframe gets cut off. I am studying how the content\'s responsiveness interacts with the fixed sandbox dimensions, considering device selection, simulated browser URLs, and the viewport\'s fixed dimensions, to narrow down specific root causes.\n\n\n**Improving Device Frame Display**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the `PreviewView.tsx` component and its device frame rendering. I\'ve realized we need realistic mockups with proper aspect ratios and bezel details. I\'m focusing on responsive iframe scaling, viewport injection, and full-height simulation to eliminate horizontal cutoffs and overflows. I\'m injecting the viewport meta tag and CSS resets to make sure things render correctly at 375px. I am going to make sure the viewport meta tag is correct.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 3
      nanos: 263903667
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
