  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Preview Environment**\n\nOkay, I\'m currently focusing on the `PreviewView.tsx` component. I\'m investigating how the live preview works within the device simulators (desktop, tablet, mobile) and trying to break down the rendering and interaction process within this part of the codebase. It\'s becoming clearer how the responsive frames are handled.\n\n\n**Enhancing Preview Rendering**\n\nI\'ve zeroed in on the `srcDocContent` rendering within the iframe. My current focus is on how to handle projects that lack proper viewport meta tags or responsive CSS, which leads to display issues in the preview frames. I am going to enhance `srcDocContent` to add a meta viewport tag and inject helper CSS for responsive styling, as well as handle React/JSX or SPA projects that may require additional rendering fixes.\n\n\n**Designing Device Mockups**\n\nI\'m now implementing realistic device mockups within the `PreviewView.tsx` component for mobile, tablet, and desktop previews, including bezels, status bars, and UI elements like dynamic islands and browser controls. I\'m focusing on adding responsive scale and orientation controls, a popout button for external previews, and a scrollable viewport for touch inertia simulation.\n\n\n"
