    thinking: "**Considering GitHub Import**\n\nI\'ve added the route `/api/github-import` in `server.ts` to handle repository imports, which will use a POST request. The `jszip` library is already a dependency. I need to figure out how to structure the data flow for both the server and client to facilitate this GitHub import functionality effectively.\n\n\n**Implementing GitHub Import**\n\nNow I am structuring the data flow for the GitHub import. The current route `/api/github-import` handles POST requests. I\'ve included error handling for missing repository URLs and invalid formats, along with parsing different URL formats to extract owner, repository name, branch, and subpath. I added authorization using GitHub Personal Access Tokens and fetch the repository metadata from the GitHub API.\n\n\n**Downloading Repository Archive**\n\nI\'m now focusing on downloading the zipball from GitHub. I\'m using the GitHub API to fetch the archive and am handling potential errors during the download. I also have error handling if it fails to download the repository archive for the given branch, then returns the corresponding error. I\'ve successfully extracted the files from the downloaded zip file using `jszip`.\n\n\n**Filtering File Extraction**\n\nI\'m now implementing the file extraction logic from the downloaded zip. I am currently filtering out certain files from being processed, like those hidden, node modules, and `.git` files. I\'m extracting text files as strings and others as Uint8Arrays. I am currently handling file content extraction and also an error condition, if no files are found.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 3
      nanos: 53664302
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
