  planner_response {
    response: "I have created and integrated the **GitHub Repository Selector (`GitHubRepoSelector`)** component inside the Import view to display the user\'s repositories after successful GitHub authentication and allow seamless project pulling into GoDeploy:\n\n- **Repository Browser & Filter Bar**:\n  - **Live Search**: Instant keyword filtering across repository names, topics, and descriptions.\n  - **Visibility Tabs**: Instant switching between **All**, **Private (\360\237\224\222)**, and **Public (\360\237\214\220)** repositories with dynamic counts.\n  - **Language & Sorting Selectors**: Dynamic language filter pills (TypeScript, JavaScript, HTML, PHP, Vue, etc.) and sorting by **Recently Updated**, **Star Count**, **Repository Name (A\342\200\223Z)**, or **Forks**.\n- **Interactive Repository Cards**:\n  - Displays owner badges, primary language indicators, star counts, fork stats, default branches, and relative last-pushed timestamps.\n  - **Branch & Subpath Customization**: Expandable configuration per repository card to select specific branches/tags or target nested monorepo subfolders (e.g., `client` or `packages/app`).\n  - **1-Click Pull Action**: Direct **\"Pull into GoDeploy\"** action button with animated progress feedback during repository tree retrieval and decompression.\n- **Account Management**:\n  - Displays authenticated user profile details, active session badges, repository refresh triggers, and account disconnect controls."
