    thinking: "**Tracing Compatibility Evolution**\n\nI\'m now tracing the evolution of the Hostinger Compatibility Score, specifically how it climbs from an initial lower value \342\200\223 perhaps 60% after import \342\200\223 up to a perfect 100%. I\'m focusing on the \"Audit & Fix\" process and the steps that drive this improvement.\n\n\n**Analyzing Initial Score Factors**\n\nI\'ve been drilling down into the codebase, specifically `analyzer.ts`, and key component views, to see why a project might start with a 60% Compatibility Score. My investigation shows the initial score is directly tied to the project source being a \"url-snapshot,\" as defined in the analyzer.  I\'m also looking into `fixEngine.ts`, and how the \"Audit & Fix\" process impacts compatibility by checking files such as `.htaccess` and `.env.example`, as well as checking languages.\n\n\n**Defining Automated Audits**\n\nNow I\'m creating an `autoAuditAndFixAllHostingerTier` function in `fixEngine.ts`. This involves detailed steps, like ensuring an index file (either HTML or PHP) with specific tags, generating a `.htaccess` file tailored for Hostinger, which will boost performance with compression, browser caching, and security headers. I\'m focusing on ensuring it addresses various factors, especially as they relate to URL snapshots.\n\n\n**Refining Auto-Fixes**\n\nI am now focused on a new tier of auto-fixes within the `autoAuditAndFixAllHostingerTier` function. This includes steps such as ensuring HTTPS/SSL redirection is ready, as well as asset path and URL normalization to ensure they are relative, which will help render the site on different hosting setups. I am also working on cleaning up hardcoded localhost references. Furthermore, I\'m working on generating `robots.txt` and a `sitemap.xml` for SEO. I am also working on generating a favicon.\n\n\n**Finalizing Compliance Criteria**\n\nI\'m now integrating crucial Hostinger hPanel elements: a `.env.example` file and a default `.env` template. I\'m also addressing Node.js and PHP engine compatibility, as well as Linux server file normalization. I will now mark the project as audited and re-run all analyses, and validation steps. I am confident I will get a 100% score!\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 4
      nanos: 250967988
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
